---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LinkBar from "../components/LinkBar.astro";
import BibtexBlock from "../components/BibtexBlock.astro";
import LimitationPresenceChart from "../components/LimitationPresenceChart.astro";
import LiveAnnotationDemo from "../components/LiveAnnotationDemo.astro";
import { BookOpen, User, Bot } from "lucide-preact";
import { authors, affiliations, paper } from "../data/paper";
---
<BaseLayout title={`${paper.title} — NLP Limitations`}>
  <h1>{paper.title}</h1>

  <p class="authors">
    {authors.map((author, i) => (
      <>
        <span>{author.name}<sup>{author.affiliation === "chula" ? "†" : "‡"}{author.corresponding ? "*" : ""}</sup></span>
        {i < authors.length - 1 ? ", " : ""}
      </>
    ))}
  </p>
  <p class="affiliations">
    <span><sup>†</sup> {affiliations.chula}</span> &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; <span><sup>‡</sup> {affiliations.google}</span>
  </p>

  <div class="venue-strip">
    <span class="venue-pill">
      <BookOpen size={14} class="venue-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
      {paper.venue}
    </span>
  </div>

  <LinkBar />

  <div class="tldr">
    <div class="tldr-title">
      <span class="tldr-badge">TL;DR</span>
    </div>
    <p class="tldr-text">
      We analyzed the Limitations sections of <strong>16,047 ACL and EMNLP papers published 2020–2025</strong> to understand how they changed over time, how they relate to paper attributes, and the writing patterns that recur around them.
    </p>
    <details class="abstract-details">
      <summary>Read the full abstract</summary>
      <p>{paper.abstract}</p>
    </details>
  </div>

  <h2>What we found</h2>
  <div class="findings-grid">
    <article class="finding-card">
      <span class="finding-rq">RQ1 · Over time</span>
      <h3 class="finding-question">How have reported limitations changed?</h3>
      <p class="finding-stat">
        Papers reporting <strong>Scope Limitation</strong> rose from <span class="stat-num">31%</span> to{" "}
        <span class="stat-num">66%</span> <span class="stat-context">(2020 &rarr; 2025)</span>
      </p>
      <p class="finding-answer">
        Scope Limitation (explicitly bounding what a study covers) overtook Methodological Constraints around the
        time the section became mandatory. This is a temporal association; we do not claim the policy caused it.
      </p>
      <div class="finding-links">
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}results#temporal-rq1`}>See the trend &rarr;</a>
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}explore?code=Scope%20Limitation&sort=newest`}>Read examples &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="finding-card">
      <span class="finding-rq">RQ2 · Across the field</span>
      <h3 class="finding-question">Do subfields and institutions differ?</h3>
      <p class="finding-stat">
        In <span class="stat-num">~97%</span> of <strong>research area × limitation code</strong> pairs, the reporting
        rate is not significantly different from the field as a whole
      </p>
      <p class="finding-answer">
        Mostly not: research areas report each limitation at similar rates.
        One clear difference: papers without large-company authors report Scope Limitation more often
        (63.6% vs. 56.6%).
      </p>
      <div class="finding-links">
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}results#attributes-rq2`}>See the comparison &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="finding-card">
      <span class="finding-rq">RQ3 · How it is written</span>
      <h3 class="finding-question">How do authors frame a limitation?</h3>
      <p class="finding-stat">
        The statement right after a limitation is <strong>Future Work</strong>{" "}
        <span class="stat-num">40.2%</span> of the time <span class="stat-context">(32.8% expected by chance)</span>
      </p>
      <p class="finding-answer">
        We call this pattern the Soft Landing.
        Also, in 2025, 90 papers had a Limitations section with only non-limitation statements, such as future-work plans.
      </p>
      <div class="finding-links">
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}results#discursive-rq3`}>See the patterns &rarr;</a>
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}explore?after=Future%20Work`}>Read real examples &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <form class="find-paper" action={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}explore`} method="get" role="search">
    <label for="find-paper-q" class="find-paper-label">Published at ACL or EMNLP 2020–2025 with a Limitations section? See how yours was coded.</label>
    <div class="find-paper-row">
      <input id="find-paper-q" name="q" type="search" placeholder="Paste your paper's title…" required />
      <button type="submit">Find my paper</button>
    </div>
  </form>

  <h2>Why there are 16,000 sections to study</h2>
  <p>
    A Limitations section was optional until EMNLP 2022 and ACL 2023 made it
    mandatory. Adoption jumped almost immediately from single digits to
    effectively 100%:
  </p>
  <LimitationPresenceChart />

  <h2>How we know</h2>
  <p>
    An LLM coded every sentence of all 16,047 sections against a shared codebook, proposing a new code whenever nothing fit;
    researchers reviewed each proposal before it joined the codebook, which grew from 25 to 50 codes. Two real sentences from the dataset:
  </p>

  <LiveAnnotationDemo />

  <h3>Can we trust the LLM's coding?</h3>
  <p>
    It was checked against a separate <strong>150-paper reference set</strong> independently coded by
    four expert human annotators. Adding the LLM as a fifth coder barely changes agreement:
  </p>
  <p class="iaa-numbers">
    <span class="badge badge-human">
      <User size={14} aria-hidden="true" />
      Human annotators only
    </span>
    <strong>α = 0.644</strong>
    <span class="iaa-arrow">&rarr;</span>
    <span class="badge badge-llm">
      <Bot size={14} aria-hidden="true" />
      + LLM as a coder
    </span>
    <strong>α = 0.647</strong>
  </p>
  <p class="section-cta">
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}methodology`}>The full pipeline, worked examples &amp; per-code agreement &rarr;</a>
  </p>

  <h2 id="citation">Citation</h2>
  <BibtexBlock />

  <p class="cta">
    <a class="cta-btn" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}explore`}>Explore all 16,047 papers &rarr;</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .authors {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }
  .affiliations {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .venue-strip {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 1.25rem;
  }
  .venue-pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    padding: 0.28rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--primary-soft);
    color: var(--primary-strong);
    border: 1px solid var(--primary-border);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .venue-icon {
    color: var(--primary-text);
  }

  .tldr {
    background: var(--primary-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--primary-border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 0.9rem 1.2rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
  .tldr-title {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .tldr-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--primary);
    color: var(--on-color);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    padding: 0.12rem 0.48rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .tldr-text {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--foreground);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--foreground);
  }
  h3 {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--foreground);
  }

  .iaa-numbers {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .badge-human {
    background: var(--green-bg);
    color: var(--green-fg);
    border: 1px solid var(--green-border);
  }
  .badge-llm {
    background: var(--violet-bg);
    color: var(--violet-fg);
    border: 1px solid var(--violet-border);
  }

  .iaa-arrow { color: var(--color-muted); }
  .section-cta { font-weight: 600; }
  .cta { margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; }

  .abstract-details {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .abstract-details summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary-strong);
  }
  .abstract-details p {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .findings-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .finding-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-top: 4px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-bg);
  }
  .finding-rq {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--primary-text);
  }
  .finding-question {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0.4rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  /* One sentence carries the number and what it measures, at close sizes,
     so the figure is never read without its subject. */
  .finding-stat {
    margin: 0.1rem 0 0.7rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .finding-stat strong {
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .stat-num {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--primary-text);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .stat-context {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .finding-answer {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .finding-links {
    margin-top: auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.3rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .finding-links a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .finding-links a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .find-paper {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--primary-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--primary-border);
  }
  .find-paper-label {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .find-paper-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .find-paper-row input {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    font: inherit;
    padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--primary-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--card);
  }
  .find-paper-row button {
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.55rem 1rem;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--primary);
    color: var(--on-color);
    cursor: pointer;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .find-paper-row button:hover {
    background: var(--primary-hover);
  }
  .cta-btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.65rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--primary);
    color: var(--on-color);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .cta-btn:hover {
    background: var(--primary-hover);
  }
</style>
